+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board delivered over a self-hosted WebSocket connection. This favors update speed and freedom from a realtime vendor over minimizing operational work: the project owns connection capacity and reconnect handling rather than paying a provider or accepting polling lag.
 
-Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery must be designed together after this choice. Polling would favor cursor queries; self-hosted sockets would need connection management and replay; hosted delivery would need publication reconciliation and provider credentials. Neither operating cost nor minimum operational burden has been declared the overriding criterion.
